What makes this document valuable?

It won't say:

"This product will earn ₹1,000 crore."

Instead, it will say:

"If the company acquires 2,000 enterprise customers at an average annual contract value of ₹X, maintains Y% retention, and achieves Z% gross margin, the business could reach ₹N crore ARR under this scenario."

That is the kind of analysis that founders, investors, and executives use to make decisions because it's based on assumptions that can be challenged and updated as the business evolves.

I would also include:

3-year, 5-year, and 10-year financial projections
Best-case, expected-case, and conservative scenarios
Sensitivity analysis (e.g., how changes in customer growth, pricing, or AI costs affect revenue and profitability)
Break-even analysis
A valuation waterfall showing how operational milestones translate into potential company value over time.
